       WEAPONS_ABSORPTION_WAVE_1.md. -->
  <!-- kotorcore/VEF/AdaptiveStorageFramework/EBSG/OuterRim Core dependencies added
       ARMOURY_ABSORBED_FRAMEWORK_DEPS_1 (2026-09-02): a minimal-list sweep (BENCH)
       measured that Defs/Absorbed_AdditionalMods/kotorcore/{VEF,AdaptiveStorageFramework,
       EBSG}/*.xml reference those frameworks' own C# classes directly (Class=
       "VEF.AnimalBehaviours...", etc.) with no MayRequire/LoadFolders gate -
       donor kotorcore's own LoadFolders gated this content on framework presence,
       and absorption dropped that gating, making it unconditional. Without the
       framework: SWPotF_RaceDef_ysalamir's whole def is discarded (unresolvable
       Class on a comp), guy762_SecretFloorPanel_BASE's ParentName misses, and
       guy762 implant defs cascade ~60 cross-refs. Separately, RSW_EWebShot's
       damageDef (OuterRim_Blaster) is defined by Outer Rim Core, not shipped here.
       These declarations do not themselves prevent that crash (modDependencies is
       advisory, not a load gate) - they make the requirement visible so
       STARWARS_DONOR_SUNSET_1 or any future donor retirement / reduced mod list
       does not silently break this content. Making the load itself resilient
       (moving these files out of Defs/ into per-framework folders LoadFolders.xml
       can gate) is a larger, separate restructuring - not done here. -->
